**Chapter 10: "The Land of the Lion King"**
**Chapter 10 Section 7: "My Friend"**

"Are you okay? Do you think you can do it properly?"

"Sis, watch your hands! Careful, careful!"

"That's the rumored silver-haired half-elf, right? Dump it on her head!"

"Don't you kids jabber at me from the side! And don't you insinuate any clear malice! It says so in the scripture too: 'Thou shalt not touch the scales of the dragon bearing unclean thoughts. The impure shall be struck by the silver rain, and until the dregs of their heart are scraped away, they shall not be permitted to pass through the golden gates.'"

"...What's that supposed to mean?"

"It means if you even *think* about doing something bad, you have to reflect on it or I'll get mad! Now, I have guests to attend to! Go play outside!"

A clear, resonant voice said this to the children, who meant no harm, and amiably shooed them outside. The children, chattering noisily, dashed out of the building.

Two boys and one girl—the girl being the one with the foulest mouth—and the fact that they were all dressed in near-black, indigo-dyed monastic robes, likely meant they were associated with the church.

At any rate, Subaru honestly thought it was nice to see them so full of energy.

"I'm sorry our children were so noisy. I try to instill good manners in them every day, but it doesn't seem to be very effective. They take advantage of me, I suppose... *sigh*..."

Watching the children's retreating backs and slowly shrugging her shoulders was the golden-haired, red-eyed nun—Filiora. Amidst preparing to welcome her guests, she had been constantly pestered by the children, and this was her lament. But truly, their attitude seemed half affection and half taking her for granted.

Anyway, before offering any words of comfort for that, Subaru and the others' attention was drawn to her precarious gait as she approached them, carrying a tea set on a silver tray.

*Rattle, rattle, rattle, rattle*—everything on the tray was sending out danger signals.

Waiting at the table in the parlor they'd been ushered into, Subaru and the others gulped as they watched her transportation efforts.

"...Um, would you like some help?"

"Wait, please don't touch me! Right now, a delicate balance is being maintained on this tray, seemingly of its own accord, and one wrong move will ruin everything. Slowly now, slowly..."

"Y-you're trying so hard...!"

Squeezing past Rem, who had offered to help, and Emilia, who was cheering her on earnestly, Filiora carefully, fearfully, managed to land the tray on the table without tipping it over.

As Subaru and the others clapped in spite of themselves, going "Oooh!", she wiped her forehead and said,

"Ahem, sorry to keep you waiting. And I apologize for making you anxious right from the start. Normally, I leave the task of welcoming guests like this to others, but right now, I'm the only one here."

"No, it's fine. Thank you for welcoming us. Actually, we're the ones who should apologize for coming when you seem short-handed."

"No, not at all. The doors of the church should always be open. The scripture also says: 'To fear and revere the Dragon's power is the mark of love. Love without reverence is arrogance, reverence without love is servility. Righteous love dwells in the nobility of standing tall before the Dragon.'"

"Um, what does that mean?"

"It means you should always be presentable, just in case someone important sees you."

Raising her index finger, Filiora answered Emilia's question like that.

That was probably a quote from the scripture of the "Dragon Faith Church," but she had a knack for breaking it down and conveying it in an easy-to-understand way. Moreover, her interpreting the stiff wording in a digestible manner was helpful even for Subaru, whose understanding of the faith was shallow.

"Speaking of presentable, was spraying spittle while dealing with the kids being presentable?"

"Urk."

"And seeing you turn bright red after you noticed us was quite a sight too, I'd say."

"Oof."

At the remarks from Subaru and Beatrice, Filiora groaned consecutively, clutching her chest. Finding her sharp reactions amusing, Subaru suddenly felt Rem at his side and Emilia at Beatrice's side, each pinching their ears.

"That was an unnecessary remark."

"Honestly, you shouldn't be so mean."

"Ow ow ow!"

Subaru and Beatrice also took damage, paying the price for their mischief. As a result, simply by bringing tea, three victims had been produced.
Anyway, enough of such joking around—

"Once again, I thank you for coming. I am Filiora... a nun of the 'Dragon Faith Church,' who has recently caused quite a stir at the royal castle."

"—"

As Filiora introduced herself, placing a hand on her chest, Subaru and the others fell silent. Seeing this, Filiora's expression clouded over instantly.

"S-say something. Otherwise, I'll start to get anxious."

"Wow, so you are aware you caused a stir."

"Of course I am. ...I am. After being looked at with such indescribable eyes by everyone at the castle, anyone would think, 'Oh? Did I mess up?'"

"Well, we weren't there at the time, but actually, I understand very well that feeling of being unbearably out of place."

"You do!? That hellish feeling!?"

"Ah, could that be referring to when Subaru insisted in front of everyone that he was my knight, and I got embarrassed and said he wasn't?"

"Ugh, exactly that!"

With Filiora leaning in excitedly and Emilia clasping her hands in front of her chest, Subaru was bombarded with innocent exclamations from both sides, and this time his old wound ached anew.

Or rather, it seemed Emilia's denial at that time was just because she was embarrassed. He hadn't exactly conducted a detailed investigation into Emilia's feelings back then, but despite the cute reason, the damage Subaru had taken was severe.

"...From what I just heard, that situation sounds unbearably awkward, but is it really true?"

"Unfortunately, Betty hadn't contracted with Subaru yet back then, so I don't know the details. But, it wouldn't be surprising if the Subaru of that era had done something like that."

"Hearing the two of you, Rem and Beako, talk about that day all over again now is seriously painful! For the record, Rem before she lost her 'memories' knew about the situation, and she was pretty sympathetic towards me, you know?"

"Are you sure about that? Perhaps the former me was simply too exasperated to comment?"

"Stop it, I'm starting to feel like that might be the case!"

Putting aside his feelings at the time, it was undeniable that his methods, approach, choice of words, and presentation had all been a series of mistakes. But he'd already reflected on that, and even though he was the one who brought it up, he wished they'd forgive him already.

However, as Subaru was being battered by his past actions—

"—I understand that feeling."

*Grip*. Two hands reached across the table and firmly grasped Subaru's right hand. Looking up, Filiora was leaning forward from the opposite side, nodding at him.

With her red eyes sparkling brilliantly, she said to the astonished Subaru,

"The cold stares from everyone around you, looking at an out-of-place person who suddenly appeared."

"—!"

"My tongue, rushing ahead with a story, unable to turn back now."

"Yes, yes! That's exactly it!"

"The silence after finishing your piece, feeling like an eternity until someone says something!"

"Those few seconds feel endlessly long...!"

"I thought, quite spectacularly... that I might have messed up."

"Filiora...!"

The terror she had experienced—every bit of it felt like his own—no, in fact, it was. Realizing this, Subaru also gripped Filiora's hand back.

Over the table, gripping each other's hands, Subaru and Filiora nodded in unison.
Yes, both Subaru and Filiora were comrades who had gotten carried away and caused a stir at the castle—

"But isn't your situation quite different? Filiora-san achieved results on the spot, whereas you postponed your chance for recovery?"

"S-stop it... We were having a nice moment here."

"Yeah, yeah! The scripture says so too: 'Beneath the shadow of the same wing, sharpen not your claws to rend your neighbor. Brothers who quarrel under the same sky err, casting aside the Dragon's mercy themselves.'"

"Um, what does that mean?"

"It means people who've shared the same embarrassment should get along instead of arguing."

"I get it! Maybe I should join the 'Dragon Faith Church'!"

"That's a delicate issue, so don't treat it so lightly!"

Just as he was about to convert due to her heartfelt empathy, Beatrice's loving slap stopped him. If love for the object of one's faith was a great motivator, then Subaru was already a follower of the Church of Beatrice, also兼任ing the Church of Emilia and the Church of Rem.

"Well, going by that logic, I'm following a lot of religions. I've always acted like a non-religious Japanese person, but from a divine perspective, am I actually a cheater...?"

"—. Well, isn't that about right?"

"That look was simply ice cold!"

The moment he muttered fearfully, Rem's pale blue eyes pierced him. Seeing Emilia and Beatrice also smiling wryly beside her, Subaru decided to drop the subject.

Having made that tactical retreat, Subaru and the others turned their attention back to Filiora. Honestly, she was already incredibly easy to get along with, but there was something they needed to tell her.
That was—

"We heard you helped Crusch-san. You might think it's strange for me to say this, but... thank you. Truly, thank you so much."

"—"

Saying this, Subaru bowed his head deeply, so low it seemed he might bump it on the table. At Subaru's words of gratitude, Filiora's eyes went wide, and she looked at Emilia and the others.

Even with the preface that it might sound strange, the reason for her surprise didn't seem to fade. However, Emilia also lowered her head to the bewildered Filiora.

"Let me thank you too. All of us really wanted to do something to help Crusch-san. And you managed to do something for her."

"Actually, we were at a loss for what measures to take. You did a splendid thing."

"I only heard about it, but I think it was truly admirable."

Following suit, not just Emilia but also Beatrice and Rem expressed their gratitude. Filiora's mouth opened and closed soundlessly for a while. Then, finally managing to process the impact she'd received, she slowly shook her head.

And before Subaru and the others, she smiled a composed, benevolent smile.

"—It's fine. I only did what I had to do. If there are people who were saved because of it, then that itself is my heart's true desire."

That reply was truly fitting for the benevolent nun Subaru imagined her to be. —If only her nostrils weren't flaring with delight, one could say it was flawless.

Of course, out of gratitude and tact, Subaru didn't mention it.

........


"I was abandoned as a baby, left in front of the church. That was a little over fifteen years ago."

With the initial greetings out of the way, Filiora began to speak about her circumstances, the situation surrounding her, and her personal history related to it.

At her opening remark about being an abandoned child, Subaru and the others couldn't help but exchange glances. —Precisely because this was the unavoidable topic concerning the suspicion that "Filiora = The Lost Princess."

"Abandoned... So you don't remember your parents?"

"No, I don't know their faces or names. But everyone at the church is my family. Have I ever felt lonely because of that? ...Well, sometimes when heartless people made fun of me, I'd get a bit upset, but basically, no. There was always someone there for me."

"I see. But still, didn you ever think it was strange yourself? I mean, blonde hair, red eyes, and the name Filiora—that's like a perfect winning hand in mahjong, or a critical hit..."

"This is the Dragon Faith Church, you know? It's natural for the Church to keep its distance from the royal family and the castle; information like that didn't reach me. ...No, thinking about it now, they probably deliberately kept it from me. Those bastards..."

Filiora clenched her fist on the table, trembling with frustration over her circumstances.

Even from this shocking first meeting and the brief exchange so far, one could tell that Filiora was quite impulsive, the type to be driven by her emotions.

Her direct appeal to the castle, which had bonded her so strongly with Subaru, also seemed to stem from that emotional outburst.

"Originally, I'd been finding the recent rampages of the Witch Cult unbearable. And then the incident in Pristella happened... That was the last straw."

"So you ignored everyone trying to stop you and stormed the castle alone."

"Could you be a little more tactful with your wording... How about, I stormed in with dignity and grace?"

"Alright then, you stormed in with dignity and grace."

"...It doesn't feel like my earnestness is coming across as much as I'd hoped."

Well, as Subaru was just following instructions, he couldn't be held responsible for the effectiveness.

At any rate, it was clear Filiora had acted out of a sense of mission and strong indignation. However, what interested Subaru and the others was the reason she was able to take that action.

That reason was—

"—You mentioned a 'Sacrament,' didn't you, Filiora?"

At the word Emilia brought up, the air in the parlor tensed slightly.

The Sacrament—that was the 'something' Filiora was said to have used to heal Crusch's body, and the possibility of overturning the Witch Cult's Authority that she had gone to the castle to demonstrate.

And for some reason, it was a means that could save the victims of the Witch Cult, which the Dragon Faith Church had kept secret and tried not to bring to light.

"—"

Wetting his lips with his tongue, Subaru tried to tame the slight tension.

Being called a Sacrament, it was probably a very important mystery of the Dragon Faith Church. Depending on the circumstances, even just knowing of its existence could make one an enemy of the Church.

If they were to delve into that, even the candid Filiora might become tight-lipped—

"The Sacrament? Yes, that's right. It's a secret art passed down long ago within the Church, and only a very few people can use it. The Church calls such a person a 'Saint,' and since I also have that qualification, I'm able to wield its power."

"Are you sure it's okay to say that so casually!?"

"Okay or not, the Church might have tried to hide it, but I've already talked about it extensively at the castle. Trying to hide it now would be pointless... The scripture also says: 'Defile not the soil cleansed by the Dragon with the poison of selfish desire. To fill a once-dried spring requires a thousand years of prayer and the tears of the guilty.'"

"Um, what does that mean?"

"In other words, if you try to gain an advantage only for yourself, it'll be hard to recover if something goes wrong. —And I thought that now was the time when something had gone wrong."

So, defying the Dragon Faith Church's wish to keep the Sacrament secret, Filiora chose to follow her own beliefs and wield its power publicly.

Of course, the Dragon Faith Church, having had this done without permission, must have been thrown into great panic, and the royal castle, now indebted to her, must have been thrown into chaos as well.

But regardless of the outcome of the chaos, the trigger was undoubtedly goodwill.

"Right now, at the castle, they're discussing how to handle me... The Church elders and my long-time family are also participating in that discussion."

"But if it's about you, Filiora, aren't you part of that discussion?"

"Even if I wanted to, they kicked me out! Even though it's about me, they said my presence would complicate things... There might have been a chance it wouldn't, but don't you think that's harsh!?"

"It's sad that they estimate the probability of it not complicating things to be so low, I guess."

"Don't be mean to her, Beako."

Blushing, Filiora protested the unfairness of her treatment, but seeing her impulsive and straightforward nature, one had to admit the相关人员's judgment was probably correct.

Filiora claimed to be fifteen, and despite her mature appearance, her inner self was indeed that of a fifteen-year-old—or perhaps even more childish. This was likely due to the influence of being raised in a sheltered way, separated from the secular world.

Honestly, Subaru couldn't fathom the intentions of the Dragon Faith Church in raising her that way.

"So, the相关人员 are at the castle? That's why Filiora-san was left alone at the church."

"Exactly. Well, I'm not lonely because the children from earlier are here, but I've been told not to wander off on my own. I want to spread the power of the Sacrament as soon as possible, every second counts...!"

"That's a Saint with a motivation I've never heard of."

She must really want to save people, but a Saint with no saintly vibe? That's something.

However, as Garfiel had mentioned at the Royal Candidate's Mansion, thinking of the victims waiting in Pristella, Subaru could only agree with Filiora's feelings. He almost felt like encouraging her himself.

"I totally get the feeling. I could ask Reinhardt to give you a quick lift to Pristella..."

"Guh... that's a tempting proposal...! But I was told to wait quietly."

"But you didn't promise, right? And even if you did, if it saves someone in the end, a little..."

"Subaru? Are you trying not only to break promises yourself, but also to make others break theirs? That's a really, really bad thing to do...?"

"The habitual promise-breaker has finally reached the end of the line."

"Guh...!"

Scolded with the implication that he understood her feelings, Subaru could only groan. Along with Filiora, who made a similar sound, they both knelt before the concept of promises.

For now, they could only pray that the discussion at the castle would conclude quickly and favorably.

"—Speaking of which, Filiora-san is a nun of the Dragon Faith Church, correct?"

"Rem?"

"Yet, despite that position, you readily accepted Emilia-san, didn't you?"

At Rem's sudden change of subject, Subaru, who had been offering prayers towards the castle, raised his eyebrows in puzzlement.

However, from the reactions of Emilia, who lowered her brows, and Filiora, who stopped her praying gesture, it was clear the topic wasn't entirely off-base.

What Rem pointed out—the relationship between the Dragon Faith Church and Emilia—its true meaning was—

"The Dragon Faith Church reveres the power, blessings, and covenant of the Divine Dragon Volcanica. And the greatest achievement of the Divine Dragon in the Kingdom of Lugnica was sealing away the Witch of Envy, right?"

"Hey, that means..."

"The more devout a follower of the Dragon Faith Church is, the more they might have certain feelings about Emilia-san... That's what I'm getting at."

Without looking at Subaru, who had stood up involuntarily, Rem wouldn't meet his eyes either. Rem, pressing her lips together tightly, was aware that her words were harsh and could potentially shatter the somewhat peaceful atmosphere of the conversation so far.

Yet Rem still spoke. She wouldn't let an unnatural situation slide without addressing it.

In fact, until Rem pointed it out, Subaru hadn't noticed the strangeness either.

It wasn't just that the Dragon Faith Church wasn't familiar to him; for Subaru, the fact that Emilia was an ultra-beautiful girl was a fresh surprise every day, but more importantly, from their first meeting to now, she had never once been an object of fear or dread for him.

But he must not forget. —Because of her origins and appearance, Emilia was constantly confronted with her similarity to the most feared 'Witch' in this world.

"—"

And that similarity to the Witch of Envy should be something that the Dragon Faith Church, which serves the Divine Dragon—one of the 'Three Great Heroes' who stopped that Witch's rampage four hundred years ago—could never ignore or simply accept unconditionally.

Moreover, Filiora was the bearer of the Church's secret Sacrament, holding a position akin to a 'Saint.' It wouldn't be strange at all, no matter what impression she had of Emilia, having been raised under the teachings of the Dragon Faith Church.

"Am I an idiot? No, I *am* an idiot."

This was something Subaru should have noticed himself, without needing Rem to point it out.

Being Emilia's number one knight, he had been sorely lacking in vigilance and knowledge about situations where she might be unfairly hurt. If that caused Emilia's expression to cloud over, was he going to just curse himself and call it even?

He had regretted his lack of knowledge, and that was partly why he had hurried to the royal capital—and yet—

"Rem, you studied up on it without me noticing. I'm really surprised."

However, as Subaru was lamenting, what Emilia herself said was not a rebuke to her incompetent number one knight, nor was it surprise at being made aware by Rem's words.

She simply smiled, grateful that Rem had chosen to bring up the topic.

"...It's not like I studied or anything that impressive. I just heard about it from big sister, since I'm also in a position where I was given a place to belong."

"But that makes me happy. Even though it means you were worried about me... it's strange, isn't it?"

"—. No, I think I understand. Being worried about can make you feel pathetic sometimes, but it also makes you feel like you're cherished."

"Hehe, is that so? Then Rem, you were cherishing me too, weren't you?"

"...I think Emilia-san was the one who did that first."

Rem looked down as she replied to Emilia, who was looking straight at her. However, Subaru could tell that Rem's attitude was her own way of hiding embarrassment.

Emilia's honest and pure gaze peeled away the complicated intentions of those who overthought things. Subaru could relate to Rem's feelings well, and he was often reminded of it himself.

"—Beako, my cheek!"

"Oh dear, here it goes!"

Right after that exchange, Subaru called out to Beatrice. Immediately, as if she'd been waiting, Beatrice slapped Subaru's cheek with her small palm—*smack*—a tingle ran through him from her cute hand, and Subaru's shoulders shook.

"Eek!? What was that all of a sudden!?"

Startled by the sudden action, Emilia gently touched Subaru's cheek. As the coolness of her white fingertips soothed his stinging cheek, Subaru shrugged and said, "Well..."

"Just got myself psyched up. A mentalism technique to reset using Beako... should we call it 'Beako-mentalism'? Or 'Beako-therapy'? Which one's better?"

"Sorry, I have no idea what you're talking about."

To Subaru's nonsensical rambling, Emilia replied in her usual manner.

Just from that reaction, Subaru could tell that Emilia wasn't afraid of the situation he had been worried about, nor did she seem insecure about his incompetence.

"Of course, I can't just rely on that and do nothing. It's pretty bad that I'm even less perceptive than Rem, who has amnesia, when it comes to worrying matters concerning our camp."

"Please do reflect on that sincerely."

"You're saying that because you believe I can do it, right? Alright, leave it to me."

"—. Well, that's fine then."

With encouragement from Rem, Subaru's flagging motivation recovered. Then, he turned sharply back to Filiora.

She was a nun of the Dragon Faith Church, a 'Saint.' But precisely because of that—

"I think there's meaning in someone like her being freed from prejudice. So, how about it, Filiora? How about forming a friendly relationship with Emilia-tan here?"

"A friendly relationship? Hey, Subaru, you mean..."

"Yes, exactly—I mean the two of you becoming friends!"

Clenching his fist, Subaru declared this forcefully. Hearing this, Emilia's violet-blue eyes sparkled, and she clasped her hands in front of her chest.

It went without saying, but Emilia was starved for friends. She had even made a friend by directly proposing to Felt, who was now a friend.

And not just Emilia, this monster of friendship-making—

"—With *me*? Become friends? Seriously!?"

*Bang!* Filiora slammed her hands on the table with a loud noise and leaned in.

Her large red eyes trembled as she looked back and forth between Subaru and Emilia.

"No, I'm sorry, this must be a mistake. Probably a mishearing. Not 'friend,' but maybe... yes, 'fiend.' Meaning I have no friends."

"Uh oh, this Saint is way too lonely."

"B-but, I think I understand how she feels. When Subaru tried to be friends with me, I was really anxious because I had no idea what he was thinking."

"Sorry for making you anxious! My feelings haven't changed from the start, they've only grown over ti— Ow! Rem, did you just step on my foot!?"

"No, I dropped an iron ball."

"You brought a morning star!?"

Rem casually hid behind her back the morning star she had dropped on Subaru's instep. He was terrified, his foot almost crushed, but the image of Rem in her maid outfit carrying around the spiked iron ball she had diligently polished while Subaru was at the mansion was oddly heartwarming.

"Hey, Filiora."

While Subaru and the others were distracted, Emilia approached Filiora, who seemed to be escaping into fantasy.

Then, as Emilia touched the hand Filiora had placed on the table, Filiora flinched and looked up at her in surprise.

"Subaru suggested it, and I'm being really lazy by just jumping on his idea, but... how about it, Filiora?"

"Wh-what, what do you mean? I'm not sure I understand... If you don't say it clearly, I might get the wrong idea. In fact, am I not already having a dream right now...?"

"No, it's not a dream. And to make sure you don't misunderstand, I'll say it clearly. If you'd like, would you become friends with me... no, with *us*!"

"—Yes, yes, of course, I'd love to!!"

Instantly, her previous weakness and meekness vanished, Filiora's face lit up, and she gripped Emilia's hands back, the two of them nurturing a new friendship at zero distance.

Somewhat overwhelmed by the speedy development, Subaru nevertheless felt the wind blowing in a good direction and nodded deeply.

"I'm glad things progressed without any trouble. But that eagerness... reminds me of when Beako finally listened to my persuasion."

"Betty's case was much more romantic and dramatic! And I wasn't that desperately starved for it!"

"Hurt, hurt—cute, cute."

Beatrice, as if unable to contain her indignation, stomped lightly on Subaru's other foot, the one Rem hadn't nearly crushed. But both the weight of the stomp and her pout were adorable.

Glancing over, he saw Rem also heaving a sigh of relief at the establishment of a relationship between Emilia and Filiora.

Even though it was a topic that needed to be addressed, it was a relationship that could have been broken off because of her. Rem's feelings were understandable.

"Are you okay with it too, Rem? The friendship?"

"I don't think it's that simple. Besides, I have Kachua."

"But isn't it fine to have as many friends as you want? I consider almost everyone I met on the Gladiator Island my friends."

"I have Kachua."

Her answer was quite stubborn. Well, how one categorizes friends is up to the individual, so it would be impolite to say too much about it.

At the very least, a friendly relationship had been formed between Emilia and Filiora. For both the Emilia Camp and the Dragon Faith Church, this might be considered a historic achievement.

"I managed to become friends with Felt-chan too, and I promised to become friends with Anastasia-san. Maybe I'm good at making friends."

Emilia herself was gaining confidence from having made several friends in a short period. At this rate, she might start approaching people on the street one after another, increasing her friend count.

That might not be bad, but it also felt like it could earn her a different kind of notoriety, so perhaps they should put a stop to Emilia's friend-seeking for now.

"Hey, wait, Emilia... may I call you Emilia? We just became friends, didn't we? Yet, mentioning the names of friends other than me seems a little harsh, don't you think? Not that I mind, of course! It's fine, really! But couldn you pay a little more attention to me, your brand-new friend...?"

Filiora, for her part, might have been friendless for too long. She seemed to have excessive expectations of friends, with slightly yandere-ish remarks slipping out.

Probably because her desire for friends was too focused on one person, it might be dangerous if she didn't increase her friends and disperse that need. If they couldn't force Rem into it, then Subaru or maybe Beatrice would have to be the recipient.

"But, really, is this okay from Filiora's perspective? I mean, the only thing my Emilia-tan has in common with the Witch of Envy is her appearance."

"—? Do you have some complaint about my Emilia?"

"Whoa, no wonder this Saint couldn't make friends!"

Pulling Emilia's arm, Filiora twirled and nestled against her chest. At this display, Subaru pressed his forehead, realizing this friendship might be more troublesome than he thought.

Amidst this exchange, Emilia, now in a position of hugging Filiora from behind, smiled wryly.

"Honestly, calm down. I'm sorry about my friend."

"Huh? What kind of dominance play is this? Emilia-tan, what am I to Emilia-tan!?"

"Huh, Subaru is my knight, right?"

"Exactly! Phew, that was close. My self-esteem is satisfied."

The rift that might have occurred between the silver-haired half-elf and the Dragon Faith Church didn't happen, but instead, a crack was about to form between the number one knight and the new friend. —It was a close call, on the verge of becoming a much bigger problem.

"—Filiora, did you kick Lusian and the others out? As proof of your remorse, you were supposed to be under surveillance, weren't you?"

Suddenly, the parlor door was pushed open, and a young man appeared.

A wide-brimmed black hat, deep purple garments—a slender-faced handsome man. He noticed Filiora and the others in the room and, with an "Oh?" his yellow eyes went wide.

"We have guests, huh? Good grief, those kids didn't even tell me. They've abandoned their surveillance duties too. I'll have to give them a good scolding later."

"Oh, welcome back, Tiger. Hey, look, this is Emilia, my friend. Isn't she great? My friend... hehe, friend, hehehe."

The young man lowered the brim of his hat, hiding his eyes. Filiora introduced Emilia, who was still hugging her, to him, her joy seeping out.

Because she was a beautiful girl, it was barely tolerable, but she looked like she was becoming addicted to friendship.

At Filiora's words, the young man called Tiger raised an eyebrow at "Emilia?" and compared her and then Subaru and the others.

"I see. I'm happy for you that you made a friend. But giving me that triumphant loo






...


――Having seen off the visiting Emilia Camp as they departed, Tiger released Filiora, whom he had been holding back.

Freed, Filiora wobbled and placed her hands on the table, her eyes lingering wistfully on the spot where Emilia and the others had vanished, searching for any trace of them. Then she glared at Tiger.

"What kind of look is that? Do you have something you want to say to me?"

"Hatred..."

"Don't just say unpleasant words like that! I had no choice, okay? It's a fact that we have things to discuss, and it's also a fact that Duke Karsten woke up."

"Hmph. The super sociable Mr. Tiger Lauron wouldn't understand."

Turning her face away in a sulk like that, Filiora then picked up her own cup of tea, untouched on the table, and brought it to her lips.

Given the tumultuous turn of events and the flow of conversation, she truly hadn't had a moment to even take a sip.

Tiger watched her profile, his yellow eyes narrowing slightly—

"Even so, of all people, it had to be Emilia-sama."

"...What about it? Don't tell me even you're going to start about the silver-haired half-elf."

"That's part of it. But it's not just that. —Filiora, the insignia?"

Asked by Tiger, Filiora looked a bit miffed, then took the insignia from her breast. She opened the palm that held it, and the crimson dragon sphere emitted a dazzling light.

Looking at that—no, looking at that light, and at Filiora who made it shine, he murmured.

It was—

"—Things are about to get busy. After all, we're a year and a half behind."
